    help
      Select the specific hardware board configuration.

config NONE
    bool "None"
    help
      No specific board selected.

config FPGA
    bool "FPGA Board"
    help
      Select this option if using the IPRO FPGA development board.

config EVB
    bool "Evaluation Board (EVB)"
    help
      Select this option if using the IPRO Evaluation Board.

config DVK
    bool "Development Kit (DVK)"
    help
      Select this option if using the IPRO Development Kit board.
      Camera pins differ from EVB (no dedicated RST/PWDN GPIOs).

config SLT
    bool "SLT Board (System Level Test)"
    help
      Select this option for SLT (System Level Test) builds.
      Disables board pinmux init to prevent output contention
      during GPIO loopback testing. UART and clocks are kept.

config DEMO_QFN32
    bool "Demo Board QFN32 (no PSRAM / no AI)"
    help
      IPRO7 SEVB QFN32 demo board (NOT the EVB). No PSRAM, no AI/NPU.
      UART console on GPIO20/21. Externally usable pins are the TB2 header
      (TB2_1..12 = GPIO 0/1/2/11/40/39/33/30/29/28/31/32); the factory-reset
      button is on GPIO32 (TB2_12). Selecting this board auto-applies its
      pinmux via board_config.h.

config DEMO_QFN56
    bool "Demo Board QFN56 (PSRAM + AI)"
    select USE_PSRAM
    help
      IPRO7 SEVB QFN56 demo board (NOT the EVB). Has PSRAM + AI/NPU + a DVP
      camera interface. UART console on GPIO20/21. Externally usable pins are
      TB0_1~12 (DVP) plus UART/I2C; the factory-reset button is on GPIO41
      (TB0_12 / CAM_CLK). Selects USE_PSRAM. Enable AI separately with
      CONFIG_AI_SUPPORT in the app .config.

config IPRO7_ARDUINO
    bool "IPRO7 Arduino Board (QFN56, PSRAM + AI)"
    select USE_PSRAM
    help
      IPRO7 Arduino form-factor board (QFN56). Has PSRAM + AI/NPU + a DVP
      camera interface. UART console on GPIO20/21. I2C0 on GPIO34 (SCL) /
      GPIO35 (SDA). DVP camera on GPIO0-7 (DAT0-7) / GPIO37 (MCLK) /
      GPIO38 (PCLK) / GPIO39 (FRAME_VLD) / GPIO40 (LINE_VLD). USB DP/DM on
      GPIO8/9. GPIO41 is the BOOT_LOAD strap; no user LED or button.
      Selects USE_PSRAM (raw per-app builds must still set
      CONFIG_USE_PSRAM=y explicitly). Enable AI with CONFIG_AI_SUPPORT.

endchoice

